==Trivia==
*The [[Time Machine]] bears some resemblance to the DeLorean Time Machine from ''Back to the Future'', as it has wheels that turn sideways like in the 2nd movie and rocket thrusters in the back.
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Into the Future's map lacks the blue tint that it has in all other versions of the game.
*In the Japanese version of the Into the Future opening, the narrator's list of ways the [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] enacted revenge on humans (sinking [[Japan (Into the Future)|Japan]], creating a [[Floating Continent (Into the Future)|Floating Continent]], etc.) consists of  ''[[wikipedia:Yojijukugo|yojijukugo]]'' (four-character compounds). This is a throwback to the Japanese version of the [[Empire of Cats]] opening, in which the narrator tries using ''yojijukugo'' to stop the Cat Army's advance.
*[[China (Into the Future)|China]], [[Jamaica (Into the Future)|Jamaica]] and the [[Moon (Into the Future)|Moon]] are the only stages to retain their positions from [[Empire of Cats]], being respectively the 3rd, 36th and 48th locations visited in both campaigns.
*[[Maldives (Empire of Cats)|Maldives]] and [[Hawaii (Empire of Cats)|Hawaii]] are the only locations visited in Empire of Cats to not appear in Into the Future, since [[Floating Continent (Into the Future)|Floating Continent]] and [[The Great Abyss (Into the Future)|The Great Abyss]] weren't in Empire of Cats, so some levels had to be replaced.
*Ironically, none of the [[Enemy Bases|enemy bases]] from Into the Future are present in its main menu background.
*On the far right of Into the Future's main menu background, you can see a freighter base which doesn't appear in any stage.
*The monkey-shaped crop circle on the map is based on "The monkey", one of the many [[wikipedia:Nazca Lines|Nazca Lines]] of Peru.
*Some of the crop circles on the map are shaped like the aliens from ''[[wikipedia:Space Invaders|Space Invaders]]''.
*In the Taiwanese version, stages 3 and 21 are Taiwan and Hong Kong instead of [[China (Into the Future)|China]] and the [[Philippines (Into the Future)|Philippines]]. The locations in between are all shifted forward by 1 (i.e., China is stage 4 instead of 3), changing the stage names, [[Treasure]] names and enemy bases, but not the [[Backgrounds|backgrounds]]. Just like in the Taiwanese version of Empire of Cats, [[Cambodia (Into the Future)|Cambodia]] and the Philippines do not appear as playable stages.
*From an unknown version to [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], a glitch made it possible to unlock [[Takuya & Yuki (Rare Cat)|Takuya & Yuki]] by entering a [[Zombie Outbreaks|Zombie Outbreak]] stage in Chapter 3 of Into the Future, closing the app, then waiting a period between 30 minutes to 20 hours before re-opening the game and completing the stage.

